# string (mathematical notation)

## docs

- https://typst.app/docs/reference/math/
- https://typst.app/docs/reference/symbols/sym/

## recipes

empty string epsilon
`$epsilon$`
`$varepsilon$`

string concatenation
`$s dot t$`
`$s · t$`

kleene star (zero or more)
`$L^*$`
`$L^star$`

kleene plus (one or more)  
`$L^+$`
`$L^plus$`

string length
`$|s|$`
`$abs(s)$`

substring notation
`$s[i..j]$`

string reversal
`$s^R$`
`$s^"rev"$`

language membership
`$s in L$`

language union
`$L_1 union L_2$`
`$L_1 cup L_2$`

language intersection
`$L_1 sect L_2$`
`$L_1 cap L_2$`

language concatenation
`$L_1 dot L_2$`

alphabet
`$Sigma$`

alphabet star (all strings)
`$Sigma^*$`

string equality
`$s = t$`
`$s equiv t$`

prefix/suffix notation
`$s sqsubseteq t$` (prefix)
`$s preceq t$` (alternative)

string as sequence
`$s = s_1 s_2 ... s_n$`
`$s = a_1 a_2 ... a_n$`
